1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,427
At the base of the leaf stalk sits a swollen joint, the pulvinus.

2
00:00:04,427 --> 00:00:11,223
When the signal arrives, the motor cells in its lower half suddenly lose potassium ions.

3
00:00:11,223 --> 00:00:17,513
Water follows them out, those cells go limp while the upper cells stay firm, and the leaf drops.

